# Build context for server/Dockerfile only.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the root
# `.dockerignore`, which is what this file is for. The root one has to
# re-include specific paths under `target/` for the enterprise images, which
# copy prebuilt binaries from there — and those negations make Docker walk the
# whole of `target/`. On a developer machine that is a ~100 GB directory, and
# the context transfer alone runs for minutes before anything compiles.
#
# This build needs none of it: it compiles from source in-image.

**/target/
.git/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

# Agent images and the registry build from their own contexts.
agents/
registry/

docs/
*.zip
*.log

# Never ship a developer's credentials into a build context.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Test and tooling output.
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
storybook-static/
.storybook/
**/__pycache__/
.venv/
